## Guides

- [Adopt agentic engineering without losing your review loop](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/agentic-engineering): Agentic engineering typically breaks in the review queue. In this piece we go over risk-tier reviews, adding an independent first pass, and tracking the metrics that hold.
- [AI agent governance: A framework for engineering leaders](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-agent-governance): AI coding agents open PRs faster than humans can review them. Learn the four governance layers that close the gap
- [AI pair programming in the agentic SDLC: When review becomes the bottleneck](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-pair-programming): AI pair programming inverts the roles. The agent writes the code and you review it, and at agent throughput review becomes the bottleneck. Here's how to keep up.
- [AI security code review: Improve code security before merge](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-security-code-review): AI security code review helps teams inspect risky pull-request changes, explain code security findings, and improve security before merge.
- [Apply AI governance to coding agents in your org](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-governance-coding-agents): AI governance for coding agents starts at the pull request merge gate. Verify agent-authored code, encode policy as config, and keep an audit trail.
- [Bring agentic code review to your existing PR workflow](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/agentic-code-review): Add agentic code review to your existing PR workflow without breaking branch protection. A practical rollout playbook with the metrics that prove it's working.
- [Build an AI second brain for engineering teams](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-second-brain-for-engineering): An AI second brain for engineering teams captures codebase decisions and review history, then applies them at review time so knowledge stays when they leave.
- [Build vs. buy a Slack agent: A decision framework](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/build-vs-buy-slack-agent): Once a Slack agent can merge code, the real cost is verification, not tokens. A build-vs-buy framework for engineering leaders deciding how to ship one.
- [Building a quality gate that works for AI-generated code](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-generated-code-quality-gate): Learn how to build a credible quality gate for AI-generated code using independence, agnosticism, discernment, and explainability.
- [Code context: The evidence behind trustworthy AI code review](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/code-context): Code context is the evidence an AI reviewer sees beyond the diff. Here's why deep context, not a bigger window, makes AI code review trustworthy.
- [Code explainability for AI-generated PRs: A reviewer's guide](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/code-explainability-for-ai-generated-prs-a-reviewers-guide): When an agent writes the PR, 'ask the author' stops being a reliable review tool. Use this practical workflow to review intent, blast radius, error paths, and evidence before merge.
- [Collaborative AI: repo rules, tickets, and review history for the agentic SDLC](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/collaborative-ai-for-agentic-sdlc): Collaborative AI keeps humans and agents working from shared repo rules, tickets, and review history so teams can trust and build on AI-generated code.
- [How to build a Slack bot that reviews your code](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/how-to-build-slack-bot-code-reviews): Learn three practical ways to bring code review into Slack, from GitHub notifications to a custom Slack bot and CodeRabbit Agent for Slack.
- [How to build an AI coding agent (and when not to)](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/how-to-build-an-ai-coding-agent): The hard part of building an AI coding agent isn't the loop or the tools. It's knowing when not to build one, and what breaks once it starts shipping code.
- [How to design agentic workflows that actually ship](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/how-to-design-agentic-workflows): Agentic workflows ship reliably only when an independent verification step gates the merge. How to design that gate, instrument the risk, and keep accountability with a human.
- [How to get AI code review alerts in Slack](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-code-review-alerts-slack): Compare four ways to route AI code review alerts into Slack without turning review channels into noisy notification feeds.
- [How to keep AI code review consistent across coding agents](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/consistent-ai-code-review-across-coding-agents): Learn how to keep one review standard across Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, other coding agents, and human-written pull requests.
- [The agentic software development lifecycle: How AI agents are reshaping every phase](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/agentic-sdlc): The agentic SDLC puts AI agents at every phase of software development. See how it reshapes planning, dev, review, and what teams need to ship safely.
- [The engineer's guide to a coding agent workflow](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/coding-agent-workflow): A coding agent workflow runs the loop from plan to merge with AI agents in it. The generation-to-verification boundary is what controls the risk.
- [The guide to guardrails for agentic coding workflows](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/guardrails-for-agentic-coding-workflows): Learn how feed-forward and feedback guardrails catch AI agent errors, enforce standards, and keep unsafe code from reaching production.
- [The practical guide to agentic context engineering](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/agentic-context-engineering): Agentic context engineering decides whether your AI code review agent catches the bug or lets it ship. Here's how to get the context right.
- [Types of AI coding agents (and where each fits in your workflow)](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/types-of-ai-coding-agents): A practical guide to the six types of AI coding agents (IDE, CLI, background, review, planning, and Slack-native) and where each fits in your development workflow
- [What are Slack agentic workflows? How they work and how to use them](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/slack-agentic-workflow): Slack agentic workflows let AI agents open PRs, triage incidents, and run standups where your team works. Here's how they work and where to start.
- [What does “LGTM” mean in code review, and when is it a warning sign?](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/what-does-lgtm-mean-in-code-review-and-when-is-it-a-warning-sign): Learn what LGTM means in code review, why large pull requests can receive shallow approvals, and how better review interfaces improve understanding.
- [What does an agentic SDLC actually look like end-to-end?](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/agentic-sdlc-end-to-end): See what an agentic SDLC looks like across planning, code generation, review, testing, deployment, and operations.
- [What Is Agentic Change Management?](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/what-is-agentic-change-management): Agentic Change Management governs software changes from proposal through post-merge maintenance when humans and AI agents both produce code.
- [What is agentic coding? A practical guide for developers](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/what-is-agentic-coding): AI-generated code has 1.7x more issues than human-written code, and volume is rising. What agentic coding is, and what it takes to keep quality from slipping.
- [What is AI agent explainability? A 2026 SDLC primer](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/ai-agent-explainability): AI agent explainability lets engineering leaders trace every AI agent decision in the SDLC to a rule, policy, and diff. Learn what it means.
- [What is AI code governance?](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/what-is-ai-code-governance): AI code governance is how teams keep AI-written code trustworthy without slowing developers down. Learn what it includes and how it works in practice.
- [What is context engineering? A primer for AI-assisted teams](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/what-is-context-engineering): Context engineering gives AI agents the right information and structure. For teams shipping production code, it's what makes review trustworthy.
- [What is harness engineering for AI code review without losing oversight?](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/harness-engineering-ai): Harness engineering for AI centers on four rings. The part most teams skip is verification. Here's how to close it.
- [What is self-healing code? And how close we actually are](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/self-healing-code): Self-healing code promises autonomous bug repair, but the gap between hype and reality is real. Here's what works in production today and what doesn't.
- [Why explainability is the new observability layer for pull requests in the agentic SDLC](https://www.coderabbit.ai/guides/pull-request-explainability-agentic-sdlc): Learn why large agent-generated pull requests need explainability, not just file-by-file diffs, so reviewers can understand change intent before merge.

